{
  // The fame of a good: three optional blocks a product may carry (see docs.md, "The fame of a
  // good"). They share one counter and differ only in what they give away.
  //
  // The counter is the amount of this good the CITY HAS GIVEN UP through the trigger below, split
  // by the quality of the units. It is cumulative and never spent, so a threshold passed long ago
  // still counts the sales of the whole game, and a save made before the blocks existed simply
  // carries no counter.
  //
  //   "trigger" — "sell" counts the units a town takes from the city, "produce" counts the units
  //               the city makes. "sell" is the default and the honest one: fame needs witnesses,
  //               and a city that ate all its own cheese is not known for cheese. Trade opens with
  //               the second era, so an early good that should be famous sooner writes "produce".
  //   "threshold" — the units the counter must reach. The blocks are absolute, not steps: 500
  //               branded units also cleared the 200 of the reputation.
  //   "min_quality" — only the units of this level and above feed the counter. Without the field
  //               every level counts. The quality of the deposits is thus the currency of prestige.
  //   "reward" — what the block gives:
  //               { "type": "trade_price", "value": <share> }  the towns pay this much more;
  //               { "type": "brand_product", "product": <id> } the recipe of a prestige good;
  //               { "type": "specialization", "id": <id> }     the branch, and a pick for it;
  //               { "type": "effect_stub", "id": <id> }       a place for an effect of the code.
  //
  // "name" and "description" belong to the challenge only: it is the one block the player accepts
  // on purpose, so it is the one that needs a title of its own.
  //
  // Every recipe that works a prestige good — the recipe of the good itself and every recipe that
  // takes it as an ingredient, the bar and the blade forged of it — is offered only after the rung
  // carrying the "brand_product" reward is paid. The game reads that from the data, so such a
  // recipe writes no gate: "unlock_challenge" on it would ask for the rung the named identifier
  // belongs to, which is not necessarily the rung that grants the good. The field is for a work the
  // fame of a good does not explain — a challenge of the era that opens something of its own.
  //
  // A "brand_of" record is a prestige good: an id of its own, never a grade of the old one. Its
  // price is the base price of the good, and the interface reads "<the base good> <the city>" —
  // the city name is composed at display time, so the data holds no name of a city at all.
